# React95 Refresh — Project Context & ADRs

**React95 Refresh** (`react95-refresh`) is a modernized Windows 95 UI component library for React 19, built with `styled-components` v6 and pre-compiled with `babel-plugin-react-compiler`.

## Directory Structure

- `src/<Component>/`: Component implementation (`<Component>.tsx`), unit tests (`<Component>.spec.tsx`), and Storybook stories (`<Component>.stories.tsx`).
- `src/common/`: Shared style factories (`index.ts`), `styleReset.ts`, sizing tokens (`system.ts`), `SwitchBase.ts`, hooks (`hooks/`), utilities (`utils/`), and 60 themes (`themes/`).
- `src/legacy/`: Deprecated v3 compatibility wrappers (`Bar`, `Cutout`, `Desktop`, `Divider`, `Fieldset`, `List`, `ListItem`, `NumberField`, `Panel`, `Progress`, `TextField`, `Tree`).
- `src/index.ts` & `src/types.ts`: Public entry points.
- `scripts/`: Consumer CLI (`link-agent-skills.ts`) published as the `react95-refresh-skills` bin. It is not part of the component runtime.
- `test/`: Test setup (`setup-test.ts` with custom `toHaveStyleRule` matcher) and helpers (`utils.tsx` with `renderWithTheme`).
- `.storybook/` & `docs/`: Storybook 10 (`@storybook/react-vite`) configuration, theme picker addon, and MDX docs.

## Commands (use `pnpm`)

- `pnpm build` — Build the ESM package and `.d.ts` files to `dist/` via `tsdown`
- `pnpm test` — Run unit tests via `vitest run`
- `pnpm typescript` — Type-check via `tsc --noEmit`
- `pnpm lint` / `pnpm lint:fix` — Check or fix code with Biome (`biome check`)
- `pnpm start` — Run Storybook dev server on port `9009`

## Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)

- **ADR-01 (React 19 + React Compiler)**: Targets `react >= 19.0.0`. Source and build pipelines run `babel-plugin-react-compiler` via `@rolldown/plugin-babel` in both `tsdown.config.mts` and `vitest.config.mts`. Uses native `React.useId` (via `src/common/hooks/useId.ts`) and DOM refs instead of legacy `findDOMNode`. All components and hooks must strictly obey the Rules of React so React Compiler can optimize them.
- **ADR-02 (`styled-components` v6 Prop Filtering)**: Custom styling props must never leak to underlying DOM nodes. Use transient props (`$disabled`, `$variant`, `$shadow`, `$fullWidth`) or `.withConfig({ shouldForwardProp: prop => !filteredProps.has(prop) })`.
- **ADR-03 (Unbundled ESM Build & Package Exports via `tsdown`)**: `tsdown` (Rolldown) builds `src/index.ts`, `src/types.ts`, and `src/common/themes/*.ts` with `unbundle: true` as ESM (`.js` / `.d.ts`; `package.json` `"type": "module"`, `"sideEffects": false`). `cpSync` copies `src/assets/fonts/dist`, `src/assets/images`, and `.cursor/skills` into `dist/` (`dist/fonts`, `dist/images`, `dist/skills`). A separate entry publishes the optional `react95-refresh-skills` bin at `dist/bin/react95-refresh-skills.js`. Public exports expose `.`, `./themes`, `./themes/*`, `./types`, and `./fonts/*`.
- **ADR-04 (Biome for Formatting & Linting)**: Biome (`biome.json`) is the single tool for formatting and linting (`src/**`, `test/**`, `.storybook/**`), replacing ESLint and Prettier.
- **ADR-05 (Vitest + Custom Style Matcher)**: Vitest (`jsdom` environment) replaces Jest. `test/setup-test.ts` implements a custom `toHaveStyleRule(property, expected)` matcher that inspects `style[data-styled]` sheets directly.
- **ADR-06 (Conventional Commits & Semantic Release)**: Commits follow Conventional Commits (`cz-conventional-changelog`) to drive automated versioning and changelog generation via `semantic-release`.

## Known Gotchas
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `.github/workflows/release.yml` still contain legacy `yarn` / Node 16 steps from upstream; local development and lockfile management strictly use `pnpm` (`pnpm-lock.yaml`).
